@startuml
title Linux Namespace Types — Runtime Configuration Selects Membership
rectangle "PID" as pid
rectangle "NET" as net
rectangle "MNT" as mnt
rectangle "UTS" as uts
rectangle "IPC" as ipc
rectangle "USER" as user
rectangle "CGROUP" as cgrp
rectangle "TIME" as timens
rectangle "Process / container workload" as c
c --> pid
c --> net
c --> mnt
c --> uts
c --> ipc
c --> user
c --> cgrp
c --> timens
note bottom of c
A namespace scopes selected resources; it is not a complete security boundary.
Types available depend on kernel configuration.
Source: Linux man-pages, namespaces(7).
end note
@enduml
